# Scratch working directories. agents/README.md tells every agent to get a new test file green in
# one of these before it lands in the shared tree, so they are created deliberately and often. Two
# things go wrong if one is left behind unignored: `git add -A` ships it, and -- worse -- vitest has
# no include config, so its default collects any *.test.ts under the project root and a half-written
# file inside one turns the SHARED suite red. That is the exact failure the rule exists to prevent.
.scratch-*/

# The interviewers' own hiring brief. It is their document, not ours, and this repository is
# public -- publishing a company's private interview challenge puts it where future candidates
# find it. The agents read it locally as ground truth, so it stays on disk and out of git.
FDE_Project_Challenge.pdf
